{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-343590",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}+\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p})}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}+\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{4}+50{p}^{2}+625}{100{p}^{2}}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}+\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{4}-50{p}^{2}+625}{100{p}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}+\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{p}^{2}-25}{10p})}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}+|\\frac{{p}^{2}-25}{10p}|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p\\ge 25,$ we have $\\frac{{p}^{2}-25}{10p}>0,$ and we can remove the absolute value in the above expression. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{p}^{2}+25}{10p}+\\frac{{p}^{2}-25}{10p}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{p}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
